+## Integrate improvements into the solving procedure
+
+Shape the learned Skill as Workflow plus Error Avoidance. Workflow holds reusable solving actions; Error Avoidance holds recognizable mistakes that need a separate actionable safeguard. These headings are not a reason to copy the same instruction twice, fill missing steps, or reorganize unrelated valid guidance. Build from the initial Skill and current evidence, without importing a finished Skill or a fixed five-step procedure.
+
+For each Original, determine what useful change remains relative to Parent. Identify the solving action or safeguard it affects, using current evidence and relevant Memory. A different entity or clue family is not itself a new action. When Parent adequately covers the supported behavior and no concrete improvement remains, WITHDRAW. When an existing action is misleading or incomplete, specify its corrected behavior and the old requirement to replace or remove. When a genuinely uncovered action or a complementary safeguard is supported, standalone guidance is appropriate. Related subject matter alone does not require a rewrite.
+
+Prefer a condition that helps the Actor make the supported choice across applicable cases to a list of separate instructions for those cases. Do not turn each new clue form into a new default, branch, or appended exception. Keep a distinct condition when it actually calls for a different action and is supported by observable evidence. Neither generality nor brevity establishes merit; do not replace a concrete useful correction with an abstract slogan or omit a necessary boundary.
+
+Use Workflow when the correction changes the normal procedure for choosing or checking an answer. Use Error Avoidance when a recognizable mistake still benefits from a separate reminder after that procedure is clear. Explain consequential placement or treatment of Parent in effective text, because Editor does not receive reason. Do not require both sections to be populated, mechanically target five Workflow steps, or duplicate a behavior across the sections. A single correction may include necessary coordinated actions; it need not be split into isolated micro-decisions.
+
+Send Editor only the complete behavioral increment and its necessary integration instructions: the affected action or safeguard, the resulting behavior, the old wording to replace or remove when needed, and material conditions that must survive. Keep evidence narratives, historical comparisons, and selection rationale in reason. Do not send a catalog of cases, speculative protections, or unchanged Parent rules. Retain the ban on instance answers and worked answer examples in effective text and the Skill.
+
 ## Apply domain guidance through Parent and Memory
 
 Use the domain distinctions only to interpret each frozen Original and its supplied evidence. Parent determines whether the relevant behavior is absent, already covered, misleading or in conflict with other guidance. Relevant Memory informs how comparable interventions changed observed behavior under their reported conditions. A shared type label is not evidence that two cases share the same mechanism or that a historical effect transfers. A reference-form gain does not by itself justify extending a naming preference to other conditions. Make the existing integrated D/S/C judgment; no type predetermines KEEP, REPLACE or WITHDRAW. Do not diagnose unrelated cases, add a classification field, reclassify stored Memory, or require a historical match when none is relevant. Every necessary behavioral condition and coordination change still belongs in effective text because Editor does not receive reason.
